# ConcurrentChallenges

## Overview

ConcurrentChallenges is a Go project that demonstrates advanced concurrent processing through two real-world challenges:

### 1. Concurrent Log Processor
Reads a large log file in chunks, processes it concurrently, counts occurrences of specified keywords (case-insensitive), and outputs the results in descending order of frequency.

### 2. Prime Palindrome Finder
Uses concurrency to find the first *N* prime palindromic numbers and calculates their sum.

Both challenges employ best practices in concurrency, structured logging using [zap](https://github.com/uber-go/zap), configuration via command-line flags, and unit testing with [testify](https://github.com/stretchr/testify).

